    "why_it_matters": "Both halves used identical protocol, identical prompts, interleaved arms, minutes apart. So this is NOT an arm/batch confound — it is genuine run-to-run variance. On this question n=10 in a single sitting can show anything from level to 3x, and FOUR separate passes at n<=10 this session produced four different answers: pilot 9v4, matrix n=3 2v2, batch A 8v7, batch B 10v3.",
    "consequence_for_this_repo": "Every result in results/ at n=10 per cell inherits this risk. Where a finding rests on a gap of a few runs in one sitting, it is not safe. The large, stable results here — benchmark-trap 0/60 -> 59/60, Q4's instruction-only 10/30 vs 30/30 — are far outside this noise band; the small ones are not.",
    "what_would_settle_it": "n>=40 per cell, or repeated sittings. Not more questions."
