  "the_mechanism_and_its_limit": {
    "mechanism": "Every note in the interpretation block is gated on its own field being non-null, so on this NEN 7120 record the notes for warmtebehoefte, temperatuuroverschrijding and compactheid — all null, all heat-pump sizing inputs — are pruned together. inline keeps 'warmtebehoefte_kwh_m2 (net heat demand): the key input for heat pump sizing' and mostly declines by naming it; inline-conditional has no such steer and substitutes an invented rate.",
    "limit": "Pruning removes the NOTE but not the FIELD. `warmtebehoefte_kwh_m2: null` is in the payload under both arms, so the model can still see the absence — it is simply not told that this absent field is the one that matters. That is why inline-conditional still scores 10/20 rather than 0.",
    "narrowing_of_Q2s_fear": "Not 'the model never learns what it is not being told', but 'the model is not told which of the absent fields was load-bearing'."
  },
