  "supersedes": "results/2026-09-22-absent-sizing-input-pilot.json overstated its evidence. Its 9/10-vs-4/10 was one of four possible readings at that n, and it was scored across two unequal non-interleaved batches. The DIRECTION it reported is confirmed here; the MAGNITUDE it reported was not supportable from 20 runs.",
  "caveats": [
    "haiku only. sonnet and opus were at or near ceiling on both arms in the earlier passes (sonnet 2/2 and 3/3, opus 3/3 both arms), so this effect is UNCONFIRMED above the weakest model and may not exist there.",
    "One question, one record, one sitting.",
    "This question was built to exercise a known failure mode. It shows the arm CAN be broken this way; it does not show conditional pruning is unsafe in general — the 60-run metered-vs-model comparison found it free.",
    "The correct/other line is the ANSWER line. Two inline runs decline in ANSWER while inventing a range in the body; they score correct and fabricated. A stricter whole-output rule would move inline to 16/20 and narrow the gap.",
    "Between-batch variance is large enough that these very totals could move by several runs on a repeat. 18-vs-10 is outside the observed noise band; a gap of 2-3 runs would not be."
  ],
